   * Fork-join pool in thread pools [02:31]
divide-and-conquer algorithms. It recursively splits large tasks into smaller subtasks using the fork operation, executes them in parallel, and combines the results using join. 
Its key feature is the work-stealing algorithm, where idle worker threads steal tasks from busy threads to improve CPU utilization. 
It's commonly used by parallel streams and many CompletableFuture operations.
